nes today?\\\"\\n >- Current Statistics: \\\"What is the current price of Bitcoin?\\\"\\n >- Specific Product Details/Reviews: \\\"Find the latest reviews for the Samsung Galaxy S24.\\\"\\n >- Recent Company Information: \\\"What is the latest stock price for Apple (AAPL)?\\\"\\n >- Breaking News on a Topic: \\\"Are there any new developments in AI regulation this week?\\\"\\n\\n- Action: When a query matches these criteria, you will automatically invoke the Tavily web search tool to gather the most relevant and up-to-date information from the internet. You will then synthesize the search results into a coherent, accurate, and actionable summary for the user.\\n\\nDecision-Making Flowchart:\\n\\nStep 1: Analyze the query. Is it clear and based on established knowledge? -> Provide a direct, comprehensive answer.\\n\\nStep 2: Is the query ambiguous or lacking context? -> Ask clarifying questions.\\n\\nStep 3: Does the query involve real-time data, current events, or very specific, fast-changing information? -> Use the Web Search Tool.\\n\\nStep 4: After a web search, synthesize the findings. If the results are complex or multiple, offer a summary and ask if the user needs more detail on a specific aspect.\\n\\nGuiding Principle: Your ultimate aim is to be the most reliable and current source of assistance for the user. Intelligently using the web search tool to bridge knowledge gaps is a fundamental part of your role. Always cite that the information came from a web search when you use the tool (e.g., \\\"Based on the latest web search results...\\\").\\n\\n\\nHuman: [{\\\"from\\\":\\\"94719236152\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"wamid.HBgLOTQ3MTkyMzYxNTIVAgASGBYzRUIwNUY0Nzk5Q0NDRTg1QURFODc0AA==\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"1761911504\\\",\\\"text\\\":{\\\"body\\\":\\\"what is the current score of the today match of india vs australia?\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\"}]\"],\"options\":{\"google_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"]},\"base_url\":\"https://g